# question: Can alarms with different technical pathways provide information about the same clinical pathway?
#
# Scope note (added after a self-audit corrected CQ4's numbers, see
# ../cq_discoveries.md's "Audit correction" entry): this query is
# deliberately narrower than CQ4's now-broader "shares a process by either
# the diagnostic OR the therapeutic chain" definition. CQ6 asks about
# MEASUREMENT convergence specifically -- different technical pathways
# independently arriving at the same clinical target -- so it only ever
# counts alarms with an actual FunctionalUnit/Sensor/Metric signature.
# Alarms that reach a process purely via the therapeutic bridge (device
# TYPE administers a modality, no Metric at all) have no technical pathway
# to compare in the first place and are correctly out of scope here, not
# an oversight carried over from before CQ4 was corrected. This is why
# CQ6's own numbers below don't match CQ4's corrected, larger group sizes
# -- the two queries are answering different questions.
#
# Filters CQ4's shared-process groups down to genuine multi-modal
# convergence: a process only qualifies here if the alarms reaching it do
# so through at least two DISTINCT technical pathways (the (FunctionalUnit,
# Sensor, Metric) signature established in CQ2), not merely because the
# same measurement recurs across several alarms at different priorities.
# Two of CQ4's five shared-process groups pass this stricter bar:
#   - physiologicalProcess:VascularCompliance -- 4 distinct pathways
#     (ABP/ABP_Mean via ABP_transducer, VenousPressure via a separate
#     transducer, PulseFlowIndex via the pulse oximeter entirely) across
#     5 alarms.
#   - physiologicalProcess:PulmonaryVentilation -- 5 distinct pathways
#     (RespiratoryRate/Volume_Minute/Volume_Tidal all via the
#     PneumoTachograph sensor, AirwayPressure via a separate transducer)
#     across 15 alarms.
# The other three CQ4 groups (CardiacContraction, PulmonaryOxygenation,
# ThermoRegulation) are excluded here: each resolves through exactly ONE
# technical pathway, just repeated across several alarms at different
# priorities/thresholds -- real co-occurrence, but not cross-pathway
# convergence, which is what this question specifically asks.
#
# ?fuClass/?sensorClass/?metricClass are each guarded with "a skos:Concept"
# -- required correctness, not stylistic: without it, `?node a ?class`
# against the OWL-RL closure returns every entailed superclass/anonymous
# restriction-class membership for that node (all the way to owl:Thing),
# not just its one real vocabulary type, which silently explodes
# ?distinctPathways into nonsense. Verified against two independent
# implementations before finalising this single-query form: a two-stage
# version (process-resolution and pathway-signature computed as separate
# queries, joined in Python) and a hand-derived cross-check from CQ1/CQ2/
# CQ4's already-established per-metric technical associations. Both agree
# exactly with the numbers above. A namespace-prefix filter was tried as a
# faster alternative to the skos:Concept join and rejected: it let entailed
# BROADER metric types through alongside the correct asserted one (e.g. a
# CO2_EndTidal instance is also entailed into the generic metric:CO2 used
# elsewhere in inference.ttl's technical axioms), silently double-counting
# a single alarm as having two pathways.
#
# reasoning: required
#
# Same known-incomplete chain as CQ3/CQ4 (see ../cq_discoveries.md):
# metric:Pulse and metric:Humidity never reach a process and are silently
# absent below.
#
# Performance note: this query joins three separately concept-typed nodes
# over the full OWL-RL closure and is measurably heavier than the other
# CQs under a naive (non-indexed) SPARQL engine -- correct, but slow to
# evaluate with rdflib+owlrl specifically. A real triplestore, or the
# two-stage execution strategy used to verify this query, should not have
# this problem.

PREFIX mda: <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#>
PREFIX skos: <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#>

SELECT ?process (GROUP_CONCAT(DISTINCT ?label; separator=" | ") AS ?alarms)
       (COUNT(DISTINCT ?a) AS ?matchCount) (COUNT(DISTINCT ?pathway) AS ?distinctPathways) WHERE {
  ?a a mda:AlarmType ; mda:hasLabel ?label ;
     mda:hasMessage/mda:triggeredBy/mda:hasFunctionalUnit ?fuNode .
  ?fuNode a ?fuClass . ?fuClass a skos:Concept .
  ?fuNode mda:hasSensor ?sensorNode .
  ?sensorNode a ?sensorClass . ?sensorClass a skos:Concept .
  ?sensorNode mda:sensorProducesSignal/(mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesSignal)*/mda:analyzedBy/mda:producesMetric ?metricNode .
  ?metricNode a ?metricClass . ?metricClass a skos:Concept .
  ?metricNode mda:approximates/mda:isPropertyOf ?process .
  BIND(CONCAT(STR(?fuClass),"|",STR(?sensorClass),"|",STR(?metricClass)) AS ?pathway)
}
GROUP BY ?process
HAVING (COUNT(DISTINCT ?pathway) > 1)
ORDER BY DESC(?distinctPathways)
